{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/301950-discipline-power-cards","id":301950,"title":"Discipline / Power cards","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-04T02:43:14-08:00","id":301950,"title":"Discipline / Power cards","content":"Hello everybody,<br /> <br /> For Requiem 1.0 I've made discipline cards (which I'm willing to share if you give me somewhere to put it online). I did it for the standard disciplines and some specific bloodline disciplines (Obtenebration, Ralab and some Cruac Rituals) my players have.<br /> <br /> Since I'll be updating to 2.0 soon, I'm wondering if anyone out there, or maybe even Onyx Path itself, has (plans for making) discipline cards for 2.0? If not, I'll work on it myself again. But in Holland we've got a saying; &quot;inventing the wheel all over&quot;. Basically it means it's a waste of time if you try to invent something that's already been invented.. Hence my question here.<br /> <br /> Edit: It's sort of similar to the Power cards for D&amp;D 4E.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4167-comedicus","name":"Comedicus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4167_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T08:24:03-08:00","id":302214,"title":"","content":"My uni gives me some server space.<br /> <br /> If you would like, I can host them for the next 1-1/2 years, at the very least (I'll graduate about then.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T08:31:03-08:00","id":302218,"title":"","content":"I'd say use Public Google Drive... that won't depend on anyone's graduation <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T09:10:14-08:00","id":302278,"title":"","content":"Aww, but I can put pretty web design up!<br /> <br /> Pretty pretty web design!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T00:57:51-08:00","id":303088,"title":"","content":"Oki, I've put it on my Google Drive thingy. Not sure if I did it right though, not really into this stuff..<br /> If I'm correct, you can view and probably download it here: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0B-SwMXjoSzSrSXh0c1lKVy05OHM&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/folderview?...HM&amp;usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> Here's a little explanation:<br /> <br /> Lightning Bolt = Instant Action<br /> Arrow pointing left and right = Contested Action<br /> Arrow in half a circle = Reflexive Action<br /> Arrow in full circle = Extended Action<br /> V: = Vitae cost<br /> W: = Willpower cost<br /> <br /> I've let the Aura Perception card of Auspex fairly empty. The idea is the PC using it can jot down the colors he knows.<br /> <br /> I know it doesn't look really cool on the computer, but if you print it, they'll fit perfectly into Magic card sleeves.<br /> It ain't perfect, but it worked for our group.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm guessing no-one has 2.0 cards?<br /> <br /> @Amechra, thank you very much for the offer. You can always get it off the Google thing and make a pretty pretty web design for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4167-comedicus","name":"Comedicus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4167_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T01:11:46-08:00","id":303094,"title":"","content":"I'd say that if you keep the cards similar, don't use the arrows/lighting bolts and similar. That place has plenty of space for a full words <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T01:18:26-08:00","id":303095,"title":"","content":"Yes, you're probably right.<br /> The only discipline that would be harder is Majesty 5, since it's instant to activate, reflexive to stop an assault and a contested roll (in 1.0).<br /> I'll see what I can do for the 2.0 cards. Don't expect to see them here tomorow, but I'll be working on posting them asap.<br /> Would be fun to make something everyone can benefit from! (Unless nobody is gonna use them anyway..)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4167-comedicus","name":"Comedicus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4167_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T01:25:28-08:00","id":303097,"title":"","content":"Well, I think they're only useful for new players, in short term games, where they need to have the knowledge asap. Or simply for new players, to have constant reminders of what they can do, So given that, they won't see use at my table <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Most likely. Perhaps one of the players would like such reminders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T11:08:12-08:00","id":307615,"title":"","content":"These rock. it would be nice if each card had a design on the other side. Perhaps I can come up with something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4135-blue-thomas","name":"Blue Thomas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4135_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T03:57:53-08:00","id":308030,"title":"","content":"May I sugest using the Discipline symbols from either the Bloodlines or Redemption, Masquerade videogames?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T05:01:09-08:00","id":308048,"title":"","content":"If you do that, could you pick better symbols for the three Physical disciplines, Protean, and Majesty? I kinda don't like the ones we've got.<br /> <br /> If I had any artistic skill whatsoever, I'd make completely new symbols for the B&amp;S disciplines. Because I'm thinking a smile (with fangs) would be an <i>excellent</i> symbol for Majesty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T07:50:37-08:00","id":314501,"title":"","content":"Hey guys,<br /> <br /> I've been struck down by a flu last week, so didn't have much time to work on it. But I already see some troubles with fitting everything on (think of Protean with all the different animal trait options).<br /> I'll try and work something out for it.<br /> <br /> Backsides would be a nice finishing touch I agree, but I'm not sure if we can freely use the symbols or if they're copyrighted or anything. I don't want to get in trouble for this stuff <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4167-comedicus","name":"Comedicus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4167_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T09:27:26-08:00","id":314625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Comedicus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/301950-discipline-power-cards?p=314501#post314501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(think of Protean with all the different animal trait options)</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you create additional condition-style cards representing each of the different animal traits? Then the original Discipline card could be simplified to choosing three of the trait cards. You'd just need to differentiate between the Minor and Major animal-traits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T00:00:09-07:00","id":1486969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Comedicus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/301950-discipline-power-cards?p=303088#post303088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oki, I've put it on my Google Drive thingy. Not sure if I did it right though, not really into this stuff..<br /> If I'm correct, you can view and probably download it here: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0B-SwMXjoSzSrSXh0c1lKVy05OHM&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/folderview?...HM&amp;usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> Here's a little explanation:<br /> <br /> Lightning Bolt = Instant Action<br /> Arrow pointing left and right = Contested Action<br /> Arrow in half a circle = Reflexive Action<br /> Arrow in full circle = Extended Action<br /> V: = Vitae cost<br /> W: = Willpower cost<br /> <br /> I've let the Aura Perception card of Auspex fairly empty. The idea is the PC using it can jot down the colors he knows.<br /> <br /> I know it doesn't look really cool on the computer, but if you print it, they'll fit perfectly into Magic card sleeves.<br /> It ain't perfect, but it worked for our group.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm guessing no-one has 2.0 cards?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1170_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1170\" data-vbnamecard=\"1170\">amechra</a>, thank you very much for the offer. You can always get it off the Google thing and make a pretty pretty web design for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for the necro. Are you able to update the link? Since Google updated all the Google Drive links, a lot of stuff that was public is no longer available, and I am desperate for some attractive, useful Discipline cards. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}